Docker Image = A Blueprint or Template (like a fresh OS installer ISO, e.g., Ubuntu 24.04).

Docker Container = A Running Instance created from that blueprint (like a virtual machine or a running isolated computer).

Just like you can install multiple independent OS instances from a single ISO file, you can create as many isolated containers as you want from a single Docker image.

