=========================


Spot on! That is the core lifecycle of Docker in a nutshell.


# Image (The Blueprint): Contains the operating system, code, dependencies, and configuration. It is read-only and static.
# Container (The Running Process): Built directly from the image. It provides an isolated workspace where you install software, run applications, or manage databases.


Everything you do in Docker—whether building a custom Dockerfile app, running MySQL, or spinning up Linux servers—follows this exact Image $\rightarrow$ Container path.













