Step 1: Check Docker is installed

docker --version

Step 2: Create a project folder

mkdir mysql-project
cd mysql-project

Step 3: Create the Dockerfile

FROM mysql:8.0

ENV MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD=RootPass@123

EXPOSE 3306

Step 4: Build the image


docker build -t my-mysql-image .


Check that it exists:

docker images

Step 1: Run the container

docker run -d --name my-mysql-container -p 3306:3306 -v mysql_data:/var/lib/mysql my-mysql-image


Step 2: Check it's running


docker ps
docker logs my-mysql-container


Step 3: Open MySQL inside the container


docker exec -it my-mysql-container mysql -u root -p   ==>  Enter the password (  RootPass@123 )



Step 4: Continue with the SQL steps


CREATE DATABASE company_db;

CREATE USER 'appuser'@'%' IDENTIFIED BY 'AppPass@123';
GRANT ALL PRIVILEGES ON company_db.* TO 'appuser'@'%';
FLUSH PRIVILEGES;

EXIT;


Then log in as the new user:


docker exec -it my-mysql-container mysql -u appuser -p company_db

Password: AppPass@123


Then create the table, insert data, and query it


